WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:16.942
When the town hall meeting ended, people returned to their homes.

2
00:00:18.223 --> 00:00:22.065
Paul Revere and John Adams stayed behind speaking together.

3
00:00:23.245 --> 00:00:25.006
The children stayed close by.

4
00:00:25.026 --> 00:00:29.528
"Paul, you know what to do," said John Adams.

5
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.121
Revere nodded and put on his hat.

6
00:00:33.141 --> 00:00:38.864
"It was nice meeting you," he said to the children and then left.

7
00:00:40.065 --> 00:00:41.085
"Where is he going?"

8
00:00:41.566 --> 00:00:42.226
asked Vinnie.

9
00:00:42.246 --> 00:00:48.729
"Mr. Revere takes important messages to New York and Philadelphia," explained Will.

10
00:00:48.749 --> 00:00:51.651
"That's what I want to do someday."

11
00:00:51.671 --> 00:00:54.452
"To be a messenger?"

12
00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:55.693
asked Vinnie.

13
00:00:55.713 --> 00:01:00.776
"To be one of the Sons of Liberty," said Will seriously.

14
00:01:02.304 --> 00:01:04.906
"Good-bye, children," said John Adams.

15
00:01:04.926 --> 00:01:08.910
"Never forget the value of freedom."

16
00:01:10.231 --> 00:01:13.013
They all shook hands, and the children left.

17
00:01:14.614 --> 00:01:18.437
As they walked down Boston's streets, the daylight was fading.

18
00:01:18.457 --> 00:01:20.679
"Come for supper.

19
00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.602
Mother is making meat stew," said Will.

20
00:01:23.622 --> 00:01:28.446
"You have been so kind to us," said Mandy.

21
00:01:28.466 --> 00:01:30.868
"But we should go now."

22
00:01:32.184 --> 00:01:33.224
"Where are we going?"

23
00:01:33.845 --> 00:01:35.065
Vinnie whispered to her.

24
00:01:35.085 --> 00:01:39.607
"Thank you for everything," said Mandy to Will.

25
00:01:39.627 --> 00:01:43.549
"Well, you know where I live," he said.

26
00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:45.890
"Visit some time.

27
00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:48.031
You can try our apple cider."

28
00:01:49.471 --> 00:01:53.773
Waving good-bye, the children watched Will disappear down the street.

29
00:01:53.793 --> 00:01:57.034
"That's just great!"

30
00:01:57.594 --> 00:01:58.375
Vinnie sighed.

31
00:01:59.775 --> 00:02:03.961
"Without Will, how are we supposed to find this tree?"

32
00:02:05.362 --> 00:02:07.583
He took the photo out of his pocket.

33
00:02:08.983 --> 00:02:10.884
Mandy was looking up the street.

34
00:02:12.185 --> 00:02:15.066
Two familiar figures were walking ahead of them.

35
00:02:15.086 --> 00:02:20.028
"Vinnie, let me see the photo," said Mandy.

36
00:02:21.129 --> 00:02:22.129
He showed it to her.

37
00:02:23.249 --> 00:02:26.211
The flag in the photo was glowing blue.

38
00:02:26.231 --> 00:02:28.752
"There's a big tree over there.

39
00:02:30.148 --> 00:02:32.810
It looks like this one," said Mandy.

40
00:02:33.991 --> 00:02:37.633
Mandy followed the two figures, walking just behind them.

41
00:02:38.954 --> 00:02:40.135
Vinnie followed her.

42
00:02:41.436 --> 00:02:46.340
When they got to the corner, the children noticed a sign on the nearby elm tree.

43
00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.541
"Can you read it?"

44
00:02:49.242 --> 00:02:49.922
asked Mandy.

45
00:02:51.183 --> 00:02:52.244
Vinnie shook his head.

46
00:02:52.264 --> 00:02:54.125
"It's too far."

47
00:02:55.646 --> 00:02:58.148
The two figures walked into a grocery store.

48
00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.623
Vinnie ran up to the tree and quickly read the sign.

49
00:03:04.084 --> 00:03:05.645
Then he ran back to Mandy.

50
00:03:05.665 --> 00:03:11.189
"It says, 'The Tree of Liberty'," he gasped.

51
00:03:12.489 --> 00:03:13.931
The two men reappeared.

52
00:03:15.251 --> 00:03:16.612
One of the men was Mr.

53
00:03:16.692 --> 00:03:17.973
Keith, the grocer.

54
00:03:19.274 --> 00:03:20.595
He held a long pole.

55
00:03:21.836 --> 00:03:24.978
The other man carried a red and white, bundled cloth.

56
00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:32.271
At the tree, they tied the cloth at the top of the pole; it was a flag!

57
00:03:33.532 --> 00:03:38.355
They lifted the flag high enough in the tree so it stuck out from the branches.

58
00:03:39.896 --> 00:03:43.098
The grocer said, "The Sons of Liberty will meet tonight."

59
00:03:43.118 --> 00:03:47.181
"Action will be taken," said the other man.

60
00:03:48.502 --> 00:03:49.683
Then he turned around.

61
00:03:50.824 --> 00:03:52.064
It was John Hancock.

62
00:03:52.084 --> 00:03:54.946
"He's been released!"

63
00:03:55.647 --> 00:03:57.108
Mandy nearly shouted.

64
00:03:58.728 --> 00:04:00.350
"Mandy! The photo!"

65
00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.451
Vinnie pointed to the picture.

66
00:04:03.733 --> 00:04:07.936
Sticking out of the tree, the red and white flag was glowing brightly.

67
00:04:09.197 --> 00:04:10.699
It was time to go home.

68
00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:16.284
The children's eyes closed as they fell into the familiar dark tunnel.
